# Stavros Realty Website - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Next.js 14 TypeScript real estate website for Spero Stavros with Keller Williams Realty, featuring luxury property listings and real estate tools.

## Architecture & Technology Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 with App Router
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS
- **Fonts**: Inter (body), Playfair Display (headings)
- **Images**: Next.js Image component for optimization

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript for all components and pages
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions
- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling
- Implement proper TypeScript interfaces for props
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure responsive design (mobile-first approach)

## Component Structure
- Place reusable components in `/src/components/`
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for component props
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Use Next.js Image component for all images
- Follow accessibility best practices

## Listings System
- **Route Structure**: `/listings` for index, `/listings/[slug]` for individual properties
- **Property Data**: Currently hardcoded in page components (future: database/CMS)
- **Components**: 
  - `PropertyHero`: Main property header with key stats
  - `PropertyGallery`: Image gallery with thumbnail navigation
  - `PropertyDetails`: Detailed property information and amenities
  - `ContactForm`: Lead capture form for property inquiries
- **Image Storage**: Property images stored in `/public/listings/[property-folder]/`
- **SEO**: Dynamic metadata generation for each property listing

## File Naming Conventions
- Use kebab-case for property slugs (e.g., `112-winchester`)
- Store property images in organized folders under `/public/listings/`
- Component files use PascalCase (e.g., `PropertyHero.tsx`)

## Development Guidelines
- Never modify `.env`, `eas.json`, or `app.config.js` files
- Always ask for permission before making additional changes beyond the request
- Use absolute paths when possible for tool calls
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Ensure all forms have proper validation and user feedback
- Follow responsive design principles

## Contact Information Standards
- **Phone Number**: Always use `(512) 661-9404` for display and `+15126619404` for tel: links
- **Email**: Always use `spero@stavrosrealty.com`
- **Consistency Rule**: All contact information must match site-wide standards across all components
- **Components to Check**: Header, Footer, Contact forms, Call-to-action buttons, and any contact displays

## Property Listing Guidelines
- Each property should have a unique slug identifier
- Property data structure should include: address, city, state, zipCode, builder, status, completion date, square footage, bedrooms, bathrooms, features, garage info, description, amenities, and location details
- Images should be optimized and properly sized
- Contact forms should be pre-populated with property-specific information
- Implement proper 404 handling for non-existent listings

## Future Enhancements
- Integration with MLS or property management systems
- Dynamic property data from CMS or database
- Advanced search and filtering capabilities
- Virtual tour integration
- Mortgage calculator integration
- Automated lead management system
